# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Mitchell Messerly et al. (2025). Multi-fidelity learning for interatomic potentials: low-level forces and high-level energies are all you need*.
#   Machine Learning Science and Technology. doi:10.1088/2632-2153/ae040b  arXiv:2505.01590v3
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2505.01590v3 (sha256 4232ff9297bfd22a...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 476 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/messerly2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: single- and multi-fidelity HIP-NN ensembles (8 models
# each; shared interaction blocks, fidelity-specific linear output
# layers) trained on the ~460k-structure ANI-1x subset that matches
# ANI-1ccx, with DFT/DZ, DFT/TZ, MP2/TZ and CCSD(T)*/CBS labels; the
# main-text test RMSEs of Tables 2-4 (ensemble means with 95%
# confidence intervals). Conformer and torsion energy-difference errors
# are derived properties. SI tables are not encoded.

